him  as having the highest number of sniper  kills by an individual in any major war  to date  seymour's reputation eventually earned  him a nickname the white death  and during the war the white death was  one of the leading themes of finnish  propaganda talking of an invisible  finnish soldier creating a hero of  mythical proportions  in 1940 seymour was hit in the face by  an explosive bullet fired by a red army  soldier  believed dead he was placed on a pile of  dead bodies  it wasn't until later when a soldier  noticed his twitching leg that he was  evacuated  the soldiers stated that half of his  face was missing  the bullet had removed his upper jaw  most of his lower jaw and the majority  of his left cheek  simul spent 14 months in 26 surgeries  recovering from his wounds  but as soon as he could he expressed his  desire to get back into the field and  serve his country in the continuation  war between 1941 and 1944  however due to the severity of his  injuries he was declined  sumo went on to make a full recovery and  after world war ii was given his own  farm in velavi where he would live until  his death in 2002  at the age of 96.  i'm a little skeptical on this one  because a couple of things don't quite  line up like the name but there are  certainly pieces of information that  follow the trend of other weapons  including the talent perfect lucky shot  which essentially means that any missed  shots returned to the magazine  thomas alexander baker was born on june  25th 1916 in new york  in 1940 he went on to join the army and  by 1944 he was serving as a private in  company a of the 105th infantry regiment  27th infantry division  on july 7th of that year baker's unit  came under attack by a large japanese  force  although he was seriously wounded early  on in the attack he refused to be  evacuated and continued to fight until  he ran out of ammo  when the comrade carrying him to safety  was wounded baker insisted that he be  left behind  his sole request was that he'd be  propped up against a tree and given a  pistol  this pistol had eight bullets remaining  and when american forces were able to  retake the position they found baker's  body the empty pistol and eight dead  japanese soldiers around him  after his death baker was promoted to  the rank of sergeant and on may 9th 1945  was awarded the medal of honor for his  actions throughout the battle  in september 1941 the london controlling  section or lcs was established  its goal to coordinate allied strategic  military deception during world war ii  after the beginning of the war the  allied nations began to recognise  deception as a useful strategy  the lcs was granted representatives from  all of the three services  and theoretically had a lot of power  but in reality there was little interest  in deception  they were authorised to prepare cover  and deception plans on a worldwide basis  coordinate deception plans prepared by  commands worldwide  and watch over the execution of  deception plans  the lcs brief cover and deception are  intended to create or reinforce a belief  in one's opponent which influences the  opponent's behavior along certain lines  cover induces belief that something true  is false  deception induces belief that something  false is true  cover conceals truth  deception conveys falsehood  cover induces non-action  deception induces action  the most significant operation with  which lcs was associated  was operation fortitude the cover and  deception for the normandy invasion in  1944  wyatt erp was an old west law man in  north america  in 1874 irp arrived in the boom town of  wichita kansas  where he was appointed to the police  force and developed a solid reputation  as a law man  but after a number of political issues  was later fired  erp began a path of moving from one boom  town to another  in 1879 he moved to tombstone where a  silver boom was underway  not long after he and his brothers  virgil and morgan clashed with a group  